# dpms-agent-m-input-verification-gate

Before composing any DPMS report, Agent M must verify all nine mandatory input categories are present; missing inputs generate FLAG-M-XX codes; the gate returns PROCEED or PROCEED WITH FLAGS but never silently omits required data.

## Procedures
- 1. Before beginning report composition, check for inputs from all nine mandatory source agents: (1) Agent L — interpretation text, risk classification, decision flags, recommendations; (2) Agent K — feasibility assessment, critical_violation flag, violation_codes, operational bounds; (3) Agent J — simulation results, expected_event_probability, exceedance probabilities, numerical_stability flag; (4) Agent I — sensitivity coefficients, ranked parameters, instability_detected flag; (5) Agent H — credible intervals (90%, 95%, 99%), uncertainty_status; (6) Agent G — harmonized_probability_grid, fusion_weights; (7) Agent F — posterior distribution, prior distribution; (8) Agent C — cleaning_metadata, sensor_data_summary; (9) Agent B — normalized_event_type, location_coordinates, time_horizon.
- 2. Also confirm Orchestrator metadata: RUN_ID, REQUESTED_FORMAT, USER_PERSONA, GENERATION_TIMESTAMP, AGENT_VERSIONS, RESOURCE_BUDGET.
- 3. For each missing mandatory input, assign a FLAG-M-XX code (starting at FLAG-M-01) and document the missing agent and impact.
- 4. If all nine are present: gate returns PROCEED.
- 5. If any are missing: gate returns PROCEED WITH FLAGS; note which downstream sections will have gaps and mark them as incomplete in the report.
- 6. Never suppress a missing-input flag or proceed as if the input were present.

## Conventions
- FLAG-M-01 is reserved for a missing Agent I (Sensitivity Analyzer) input.
- Gate result of PROCEED WITH FLAGS does not block composition — it documents gaps and proceeds.
- Missing sensitivity data results in a proxy chart or placeholder section, not a silent omission.

